From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:04:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: threads and synchronisation,
 nn::fs/account/oe/vi, the NVN device, generated trivial overrides

Guest threads are Python threads running the recompiled code; a Horizon mutex word and condition variable (ArbitrateLock/Unlock, WaitProcessWideKeyAtomic/Signal), events and waits with timeouts. nn::fs over the RomFS image and host directories, nn::account, nn::oe, nn::vi and nv::, ported from engine/dm/host/hle_*.c; 259 trivial HLE_FORCE entries generated from the C sources (gen_trivial_overrides.py). The NVN device (horizon_nvn.py, nvn_layout.py): Tegra X1 limits, pools, buffers, texture storage sizes, queues, command buffers replayed at submit (render targets, clears), the window presented through horizon_display. Found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: S7bis Linux Horizon layer and AOT support found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2; tests use synthetic code and fake guest memory, no game data
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

